<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tagaung Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">850 BCE – 100 CE (approx.) · capital Tagaung</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The legendary first kingdom of the Burmese chronicles, placed at Tagaung on the upper Irrawaddy and claimed as the ancestral seat of Burmese kingship.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Burmese chronicles, compiled many centuries later, say that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abhiraja">Abhiraja</a>, a prince of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sakya-regime">Sakya</a> clan of the Buddha, migrated from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and founded Tagaung on the east bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irrawaddy-river">Irrawaddy</a>, traditionally dated to the 9th century BCE. Archaeology at the site shows a walled settlement of the early first millennium CE, associated with Pyu-style culture, but nothing confirms the chronicle dates.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Almost nothing reliable is known about its government. The chronicles give a long list of kings descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abhiraja">Abhiraja</a> and say the realm was overrun by raiders from the north, after which a branch of the royal line moved south to found <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sri-ksetra-kingdom">Sri Ksetra</a>. Excavated brick walls, burial urns and pottery point to a modest urban centre linked to the Pyu world.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The chronicle account ends with Tagaung's fall and the migration of its princes, a story that later Burmese dynasties used to connect themselves to the Buddha's family. Tagaung survived as a town, and its place in royal genealogy gave it lasting symbolic weight in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ava-kingdom">Ava Kingdom</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/konbaung-dynasty">Konbaung dynasty</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tagaung-kingdom.jpg" alt="Tagaung Kingdom" width="264" height="583"><figcaption>Image: Hybernator · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pyu_Realm.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>850 BCE – 100 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tagaung</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abhiraja</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Myanmar</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Tagaung</dd></dl></aside></div>

